#: ../../source/templates_voltagent.md:16
msgid "1. Visual Theme & Atmosphere"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_voltagent.md:18
msgid ""
"VoltAgent's interface is a deep-space command terminal for the AI age — a"
" developer-facing darkness built on near-pure-black surfaces (`#050507`) "
"where the only interruption is the electric pulse of emerald green "
"energy. The entire experience evokes the feeling of staring into a high-"
"powered IDE at 2am: dark, focused, and alive with purpose. This is not a "
"friendly SaaS landing page — it's an engineering platform that announces "
"itself through code snippets, architectural diagrams, and raw technical "
"confidence."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_voltagent.md:20
msgid ""
"The green accent (`#00d992`) is used with surgical precision — it glows "
"from headlines, borders, and interactive elements like a circuit board "
"carrying a signal. Against the carbon-black canvas, this green reads as "
"\"power on\" — a deliberate visual metaphor for an AI agent engineering "
"platform. The supporting palette is built entirely from warm-neutral "
"grays (`#3d3a39`, `#8b949e`, `#b8b3b0`) that soften the darkness without "
"introducing color noise, creating a cockpit-like warmth that pure blue-"
"grays would lack."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_voltagent.md:22
msgid ""
"Typography leans on the system font stack for headings — achieving "
"maximum rendering speed and native-feeling authority — while Inter "
"carries the body and UI text with geometric precision. Code blocks use "
"SFMono-Regular, the same font developers see in their terminals, "
"reinforcing the tool's credibility at every scroll."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_voltagent.md:24
msgid "**Key Characteristics:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_voltagent.md:25
msgid ""
"Carbon-black canvas (`#050507`) with warm-gray border containment "
"(`#3d3a39`) — not cold or sterile"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_voltagent.md:26
msgid ""
"Single-accent identity: Emerald Signal Green (`#00d992`) as the sole "
"chromatic energy source"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_voltagent.md:27
msgid ""
"Dual-typography system: system-ui for authoritative headings, Inter for "
"precise UI/body text, SFMono for code credibility"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_voltagent.md:28
msgid ""
"Ultra-tight heading line-heights (1.0–1.11) creating dense, compressed "
"power blocks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_voltagent.md:29
msgid ""
"Warm neutral palette (`#3d3a39`, `#8b949e`, `#b8b3b0`) that prevents the "
"dark theme from feeling clinical"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_voltagent.md:30
msgid "Developer-terminal aesthetic where code snippets ARE the hero content"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_voltagent.md:31
msgid ""
"Green glow effects (`drop-shadow`, border accents) that make UI elements "
"feel electrically alive"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_voltagent.md:33
msgid "2. Color Palette & Roles"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_voltagent.md:35
msgid "Primary"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_voltagent.md:36
msgid ""
"**Emerald Signal Green** (`#00d992`): The core brand energy — used for "
"accent borders, glow effects, and the highest-signal interactive moments."
" This is the \"power-on\" indicator of the entire interface."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_voltagent.md:37
msgid ""
"**VoltAgent Mint** (`#2fd6a1`): The button-text variant of the brand "
"green — slightly warmer and more readable than pure Signal Green, used "
"specifically for CTA text on dark surfaces."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_voltagent.md:38
msgid ""
"**Tailwind Emerald** (`#10b981`): The ecosystem-standard green used at "
"low opacity (30%) for subtle background tints and link defaults. Bridges "
"VoltAgent's custom palette with Tailwind's utility classes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_voltagent.md:40
msgid "Secondary & Accent"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_voltagent.md:41
msgid ""
"**Soft Purple** (`#818cf8`): A cool indigo-violet used sparingly for "
"secondary categorization, code syntax highlights, and visual variety "
"without competing with green."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_voltagent.md:42
msgid ""
"**Cobalt Primary** (`#306cce`): Docusaurus primary dark — used in "
"documentation contexts for links and interactive focus states."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_voltagent.md:43
msgid ""
"**Deep Cobalt** (`#2554a0`): The darkest primary shade, reserved for "
"pressed/active states in documentation UI."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_voltagent.md:44
#, python-format
msgid ""
"**Ring Blue** (`#3b82f6`): Tailwind's ring color at 50% opacity — visible"
" only during keyboard focus for accessibility compliance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_voltagent.md:46
msgid "Surface & Background"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_voltagent.md:47
msgid ""
"**Abyss Black** (`#050507`): The landing page canvas — a near-pure black "
"with the faintest warm undertone, darker than most \"dark themes\" for "
"maximum contrast with green accents."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_voltagent.md:48
msgid ""
"**Carbon Surface** (`#101010`): The primary card and button background — "
"one shade lighter than Abyss, creating a barely perceptible elevation "
"layer. Used across all contained surfaces."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_voltagent.md:49
msgid ""
"**Warm Charcoal Border** (`#3d3a39`): The signature containment color — "
"not a cold gray but a warm, almost brownish dark tone that prevents "
"borders from feeling harsh against the black canvas."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_voltagent.md:51
msgid "Neutrals & Text"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_voltagent.md:52
msgid ""
"**Snow White** (`#f2f2f2`): The primary text color on dark surfaces — not"
" pure white (`#ffffff`) but a softened, eye-friendly off-white. The most-"
"used color on the site (1008 instances)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_voltagent.md:53
msgid ""
"**Pure White** (`#ffffff`): Reserved for the highest-emphasis moments — "
"ghost button text and maximum-contrast headings. Used at low opacity (5%)"
" for subtle overlay effects."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_voltagent.md:54
msgid ""
"**Warm Parchment** (`#b8b3b0`): Secondary body text — a warm light gray "
"with a slight pinkish undertone that reads as \"paper\" against the dark "
"canvas."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_voltagent.md:55
msgid ""
"**Steel Slate** (`#8b949e`): Tertiary text, metadata, timestamps, and de-"
"emphasized content. A cool blue-gray that provides clear hierarchy below "
"Warm Parchment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_voltagent.md:56
msgid ""
"**Fog Gray** (`#bdbdbd`): Footer links and supporting navigation text — "
"brightens on hover to Pure White."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_voltagent.md:57
msgid ""
"**Mist Gray** (`#dcdcdc`): Slightly brighter than Fog, used for secondary"
" link text that transitions to bright green on hover."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_voltagent.md:58
msgid ""
"**Near White** (`#eeeeee`): Highest-contrast secondary text, one step "
"below Snow White."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_voltagent.md:60
msgid "Semantic & Accent"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_voltagent.md:61
msgid ""
"**Success Emerald** (`#008b00`): Deep green for success states and "
"positive confirmations in documentation contexts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_voltagent.md:62
msgid ""
"**Success Light** (`#80d280`): Soft pastel green for success backgrounds "
"and subtle positive indicators."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_voltagent.md:63
msgid ""
"**Warning Amber** (`#ffba00`): Bright amber for warning alerts and "
"caution states."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_voltagent.md:64
msgid "**Warning Pale** (`#ffdd80`): Softened amber for warning background fills."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_voltagent.md:65
msgid ""
"**Danger Coral** (`#fb565b`): Vivid red for error states and destructive "
"action warnings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_voltagent.md:66
msgid "**Danger Rose** (`#fd9c9f`): Softened coral-pink for error backgrounds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_voltagent.md:67
msgid ""
"**Info Teal** (`#4cb3d4`): Cool teal-blue for informational callouts and "
"tip admonitions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_voltagent.md:68
msgid ""
"**Dashed Border Slate** (`#4f5d75` at 40%): A muted blue-gray used "
"exclusively for decorative dashed borders in workflow diagrams."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_voltagent.md:70
msgid "Gradient System"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_voltagent.md:71
msgid ""
"**Green Signal Glow**: `drop-shadow(0 0 2px #00d992)` animating to `drop-"
"shadow(0 0 8px #00d992)` — creates a pulsing \"electric charge\" effect "
"on the VoltAgent bolt logo and interactive elements. The glow expands and"
" contracts like a heartbeat."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_voltagent.md:72
msgid ""
"**Warm Ambient Haze**: `rgba(92, 88, 85, 0.2) 0px 0px 15px` — a warm-"
"toned diffused shadow that creates a soft atmospheric glow around "
"elevated cards, visible at the edges without sharp boundaries."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_voltagent.md:73
msgid ""
"**Deep Dramatic Elevation**: `rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.7) 0px 20px 60px` with "
"`rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.1) 0px 0px 0px 1px inset` — a heavy, dramatic "
"downward shadow paired with a faint inset slate ring for the most "
"prominent floating elements."
msgstr ""

