#: ../../source/templates_voltagent.md:102
msgid "Principles"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_voltagent.md:103
msgid ""
"**System-native authority**: Display headings use system-ui rather than a"
" custom web font — this means the largest text renders instantly (no "
"FOIT/FOUT) and inherits the operating system's native personality. On "
"macOS it's SF Pro, on Windows it's Segoe UI. The design accepts this "
"variability as a feature, not a bug."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_voltagent.md:104
msgid ""
"**Tight compression creates density**: Hero line-heights are extremely "
"compressed (1.0) with negative letter-spacing (-0.65px to -0.9px), "
"creating text blocks that feel like dense technical specifications rather"
" than airy marketing copy."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_voltagent.md:105
msgid ""
"**Weight gradient, not weight contrast**: The system uses a gentle "
"300→400→500→600→700 weight progression. Bold (700) is reserved for sub-"
"headings and code-button emphasis. Most body text lives at 400–500, "
"creating subtle rather than dramatic hierarchy."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_voltagent.md:106
msgid ""
"**Uppercase is earned and wide**: When uppercase appears, it's always "
"paired with generous letter-spacing (0.45px–2.52px), transforming dense "
"words into spaced-out overline labels. This treatment is never applied to"
" headings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_voltagent.md:107
msgid ""
"**OpenType by default**: Both system-ui and Inter enable `\"calt\"` and "
"`\"rlig\"` features, ensuring contextual character adjustments and "
"ligature rendering throughout."
msgstr ""

